description:
Follow-up to nostrc-s2bz (kind 443 -> 30443 on branch feat/marmot-keypackage-30443). libmarmot now emits and parses kind:30443 in the MDK 0.8 transport profile pinned by libmarmot/tests/vectors/mdk/protocol-vectors.json. The ADOPTED Marmot spec (marmot-protocol/marmot @26fa6a6: transports/nostr.md 'KeyPackage publication', foundation/key-packages.md) is a stricter cutover profile that libmarmot does not meet yet:
1) content must be base64 of an MLSMessage with wire_format=mls_key_package, not a bare KeyPackage (KeyPackageRef is still computed over the inner KeyPackage);
2) a sender MUST NOT add an 'encoding' tag, and KeyPackage events do not carry 'relays' (discovery goes through kind 10002 write relays);
3) a required 'app_components' id-list tag must include 0x8009, and every KeyPackage LeafNode must carry marmot.member.account-identity-proof.v2 in its app_data_dictionary;
4) a Lifetime extension is required, must be current at validation time, and not_after - not_before must be <= 7,261,200 s (libmarmot only checks ordering);
5) last-resort status moves to an app_data_dictionary entry.
Reference implementation: MDK master crates/transport-nostr-adapter/src/key_package.rs and crates/marmot-app/src/key_package_records.rs ('strict cutover rejects legacy KeyPackages').
Needs a profile/version decision: the MDK 0.8 vectors (encoding+relays, raw KeyPackage) conflict with the adopted rules, so new adopted-profile vectors are required. This is Groundhog W2 scope (docs/plans/groundhog-gnome-messaging-2026-09-25.md).
